# Lesson 2, new hand: a 3NT opening (23-25, balanced).
title: Open 3NT with 24
id: L02-18
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.2
student: S
board: 18
dealer: E
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  9742   T83    95     Q873
  E  QJ8    A642   86     T962
  S  AK5    KQ5    AKJ7   KJ4
  W  T63    J97    QT432  A5

auction:
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = 23-25 points, balanced
     key: 24 HCP and balanced: open 3NT.
     not 2NT: 2NT shows 21-22. Did you count 24?
     not 2D: A two-bid needs a five-card suit. With a balanced 23-25, open 3NT.
     not 1D: With 24 points, a one-bid might be passed out. Which opening shows your hand in one go?
     not *: With a balanced 23-25, open 3NT.
  W Pass
  N Pass   = 2 points: nothing to add
  E Pass

auction recap:
  3NT describes a balanced 23-25 in a single bid. Partner has only 2
  points, so he passes. You are declarer, because you bid no-trump first,
  and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W D3  N D9  E D6  S D7
      note: Dummy's ♦9 wins the first trick.
  2   N H3  E H2  S HQ  W H7
      note: The plan: drive out the ♣A, keeping your other suits as stoppers. First use dummy's entry to lead a heart toward your ♥KQ.
  3   S CK  W CA  N C3  E C2
      note: Now drive out the ♣A.
  4   W HJ  N H8  E H4  S HK
  5   S CJ  W C5  N C7  E C6
      note: Your clubs are winners now.
  6   S C4  W D2  N CQ  E C9
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q.
  7   N S2  E SJ  S SA  W S3
      note: Back to your ♠A.
  8   S SK  W S6  N S4  E S8
      note: The ♠K.
  9   S DA  W D4  N D5  E D8
      note: The ♦A.
  10  S DK  W DT  N HT  E CT
      note: The ♦K.
  11  S DJ  W DQ  N S7  E H6
      note: Nine tricks are in. Your ♦J loses to West's queen.
  12  W H9  N C8  E HA  S H5
  13  E SQ  S S5  W ST  N S9
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  The plan: drive out the ♣A, keeping your other suits as stoppers.

  3NT made. Partner had almost nothing, but your 24 points and his 2 were
  just enough.
